# Meta Conversions API — read docs first

Before writing or changing Meta Conversions API (server-side events) or related tracking code, **fetch and read the live Meta docs**. Do not rely on memory alone.

## Required starting point

- [Conversions API overview](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/conversions-api)

## Follow these pages as needed

1. [Get Started](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/conversions-api/get-started)
2. [Using the API](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/conversions-api/using-the-api) (POST requests, batching, event time)
3. [Verifying setup](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/conversions-api/verifying-setup)
4. [API Parameters](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/conversions-api/parameters)
5. [Best practices](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/conversions-api/best-practices)
6. [Payload Helper](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/conversions-api/payload-helper)
7. [Troubleshooting](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/conversions-api/support)

## Rule

- Open the overview, then open the linked pages that match the task.
- Match Meta’s current payload shape, parameters, and verification steps.
- Prefer Meta’s docs over older blog posts or outdated examples.
